#
# Conformance case: common-logic/universal-implication.
#
# ISO 24707 (Common Logic) example — a universally quantified material implication:
#   CLIF:  (forall (x) (if (Man x) (Mortal x)))
# "Every man is mortal." Encoded as the canonical logic: full-FOL Formula AST (a
# Forall over an Implies of two unary atoms). This case gates the CLIF/CGIF/XCL Exact
# projections: the IR must round-trip through each dialect with IR isomorphism, and the
# three reconstructions must be cross-dialect equivalent (CLIF ≡ CGIF ≡ XCL).

